> > I am currently using DISTANCE 5 to analyse some bird survey data from
> > rainforest in Northern Australia.  At the moment I am concentrating on
> > estimating total abundance for a species which is largely restricted
> > to upland forests.  My data are distances to birds from survey
> > transects in forests at different altitudes  (for which I have
> > estimates of total areas of forest)  My question is:  When using
> > DISTANCE to estimate their total abundance in each stratum, I ought to
> > include those surveys at lower altitudes where the birds are at lower
> > abundance, including those surveys that failed to detect any.  if I
> > include these as simply surveys with blanks where perp_distance should
> > be, is this achieved?  If so,  I would like some help understanding
